  "description": "Krea 2 Turbo text-to-image. An 8-step distilled DiT (cfg 1.0, euler/simple) with a Qwen3-VL 4B text encoder and the Qwen-Image VAE \u2014 around 13 GB of diffusion weights plus a 5 GB encoder, so 16 GB VRAM or more. Nine official style LoRAs are exposed through the `style` input, which selects the LoRA file, rewires the sampler onto the LoRA loader, and appends the LoRA's trigger word to your prompt (the editor's CustomCombo plumbing that normally does this does not run over the API). Output size comes from a ResolutionSelector: `aspect_ratio` picks the shape, `resolution` the 1-2 MP budget. Derived from Comfy-Org's image_krea2_turbo_t2i template with the subgraph flattened and the in-workflow LLM prompt enhancement removed \u2014 Claude writes the prompt, so a second model should not rewrite it.",
